---
/**
 * FedFastedTimeline — "time since your last meal." The other islands sit inside one pathway;
 * this one zooms all the way out to the whole-body fuel economy and lets you scrub time. Drag
 * the slider from a fresh meal out to five weeks of fasting and watch who pays for blood glucose:
 * the plate, then liver glycogen and new glucose together (about half each overnight), then
 * almost all new glucose, stretched by ketones. The time axis is linear for the first three days
 * and compressed from day 3 to week 5. The insulin : glucagon ratio flips with it, four organs —
 * liver, adipose, muscle, brain — change what they burn and export, and a "new glucose carbon"
 * line keeps the accounting honest (lactate only recycles; glycerol and amino acids are new).
 * The payoff is the brain's slow pivot to ketone bodies over days to weeks, the adaptation that
 * spares muscle protein in a long fast. Self-contained vanilla-TS Astro island. Original.
 */
---

<figure class="fft card" data-fedfast>
  <figcaption class="fft-head">Time since your last meal — how the body switches fuels<span class="fft-chip">⚙ original · interactive</span></figcaption>

  <svg class="fft-svg" viewBox="0 0 460 208" role="img" aria-label="Schematic timeline from a meal to five weeks of fasting: blood glucose is supplied first by the meal, then by liver glycogen and new glucose together, then almost entirely by new glucose; blood ketone bodies rise to about 2 to 3 mM by day three and 7 to 8 mM by five weeks, when the brain burns about two-thirds ketones" data-svg></svg>

  <label class="fft-slabel"><span>Drag to set the time since your last meal: <em data-out="time">0 h</em></span>
    <input type="range" data-in="time" min="0" max="200" step="1" value="0" />
  </label>

  <div class="fft-state" role="status">
    <span class="fft-statename" data-name></span>
    <span class="fft-hormone" data-hormone></span>
  </div>
  <p class="fft-glucose" data-glucose></p>
  <p class="fft-carbon"><span class="fft-carbon-k">New glucose carbon from:</span> <span data-carbon></span></p>

  <div class="fft-organs">
    <div class="fft-organ"><span class="fft-o-name">Liver</span><span class="fft-o-job" data-liver></span></div>
    <div class="fft-organ"><span class="fft-o-name">Adipose</span><span class="fft-o-job" data-adipose></span></div>
    <div class="fft-organ"><span class="fft-o-name">Muscle</span><span class="fft-o-job" data-muscle></span></div>
    <div class="fft-organ"><span class="fft-o-name">Brain</span><span class="fft-o-job" data-brain></span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="fft-foot">The body never lets blood glucose drift far — it just keeps changing who pays for it. First the meal covers the bill; then liver glycogen and new glucose share it, about half each overnight; by the second or third day it is almost all new glucose. The stages blend. New glucose is built from the glycerol off your fat and amino acids pulled from muscle (lactate only recycles carbon the body already had). Run that too long and you would burn through your own muscle. The escape hatch is ketogenesis: the liver ships ketone bodies the brain learns to burn, cutting its glucose need from roughly 120 to 40 grams a day over days to weeks. That protein-sparing adaptation is what makes a long fast survivable.</p>
</figure>

<script>
  const ACCENT = '#0e7c86', NAVY = '#232d4b', ORANGE = '#e57200', GOLD = '#D4A843', PLUM = '#5b4a8a';
  const SVGNS = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
  function el(name: string, attrs: Record<string, string | number>): SVGElement {
    const e = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, name);
    for (const k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, String(attrs[k]));
    return e;
  }

  type State = {
    name: string; color: string; hormone: string; glucose: string; carbon: string;
    liver: string; adipose: string; muscle: string; brain: string;
  };
  const H3D = 72, H5W = 840; // 3 days and 5 weeks, in hours
  // whole-body states keyed by hours since eating (rows of the lesson's fast table)
  function stateFor(h: number): State {
    if (h < 4) return {
      name: 'FED · absorptive', color: ORANGE,
      hormone: 'Insulin : glucagon — high',
      glucose: 'Keeping blood glucose up right now: the meal itself — dietary carbohydrate is still being absorbed.',
      carbon: 'none needed; the meal supplies the glucose.',
      liver: 'Storing glycogen; can also turn surplus glucose into fat.',
      adipose: 'Storing incoming fat, mostly from the meal, as triglyceride.',
      muscle: 'Taking up glucose and topping off its own glycogen.',
      brain: 'Burning glucose, as always.',
    };
    if (h < 16) return {
      name: 'OVERNIGHT FAST', color: GOLD,
      hormone: 'Insulin : glucagon — falling',
      glucose: 'Keeping blood glucose up right now: liver glycogen and new glucose (gluconeogenesis) together, about half each by the end of an overnight fast.',
      carbon: 'glycerol + amino acids (lactate only recycles).',
      liver: 'Breaking down glycogen and already making new glucose; exporting both.',
      adipose: 'Beginning to release fatty acids as insulin falls.',
      muscle: 'Shifting toward burning fatty acids to spare glucose.',
      brain: 'Still glucose only.',
    };
    if (h < 24) return {
      name: 'OVERNIGHT FAST', color: GOLD,
      hormone: 'Insulin : glucagon — falling',
      glucose: 'Keeping blood glucose up right now: mostly new glucose (gluconeogenesis); liver glycogen is running down.',
      carbon: 'glycerol + amino acids (lactate only recycles).',
      liver: 'Making more and more new glucose as its glycogen runs down.',
      adipose: 'Releasing more fatty acids as insulin keeps falling.',
      muscle: 'Burning mostly fatty acids, sparing glucose for the brain.',
      brain: 'Still glucose only.',
    };
    if (h < H3D) return {
      name: 'FASTING', color: ACCENT,
      hormone: 'Insulin : glucagon — low',
      glucose: 'Keeping blood glucose up right now: mostly new glucose (gluconeogenesis); glycogen is nearly spent.',
      carbon: 'glycerol + amino acids (lactate only recycles).',
      liver: 'Gluconeogenesis: new glucose from glycerol and amino acids (new carbon), plus lactate recycled from red cells and muscle. Ketone-body output is climbing.',
      adipose: 'Lipolysis in full swing, flooding the blood with free fatty acids.',
      muscle: 'Burning fatty acids and ketones, sparing glucose for the brain — and breaking down protein to send amino acids (as alanine) to the liver.',
      brain: 'Still mostly glucose, but ketone use is starting to climb.',
    };
    if (h < 14 * 24) return {
      name: 'PROLONGED FAST · days', color: PLUM,
      hormone: 'Insulin : glucagon — low',
      glucose: 'Keeping blood glucose up right now: new glucose only, from the liver and, more and more, the kidney.',
      carbon: 'glycerol + amino acids, kidney\u2019s share rising.',
      liver: 'Ketogenesis in full swing: fatty acids become ketone bodies for export, while gluconeogenesis continues.',
      adipose: 'Sustained lipolysis — fat is now the body\u2019s main fuel reserve.',
      muscle: 'Burning fatty acids and ketones; protein breakdown near its peak at about day three, then falling as ketones spare it.',
      brain: 'Glucose, with more and more ketone bodies. Over days to weeks this cuts its glucose need from about 120 to about 40 g a day.',
    };
    return {
      name: 'PROLONGED FAST · weeks', color: NAVY,
      hormone: 'Insulin : glucagon — low',
      glucose: 'Keeping blood glucose up right now: new glucose only, with the kidney now making about as much as the liver.',
      carbon: 'same, but far less protein needed as ketones feed the brain.',
      liver: 'Making ketone bodies (blood levels about 7\u20138 mM) and less glucose than early in the fast.',
      adipose: 'Sustained lipolysis — fat is the body\u2019s main fuel reserve.',
      muscle: 'Burning mostly fatty acids; protein breakdown well below its day-three peak.',
      brain: 'About two-thirds ketone bodies; its glucose need is down to roughly 40 g a day, so far less muscle protein is spent.',
    };
  }

  // Time axis: linear for 0-72 h across the left 60% of the plot, then 3 d-5 wk compressed
  // (log time) into the right 40%. The slider runs 0-200 in the same fraction, so it tracks the plot.
  const LSPAN = Math.log(H5W / H3D);
  const frac = (h: number) => (h <= H3D ? 0.6 * h / H3D : 0.6 + 0.4 * Math.log(h / H3D) / LSPAN);
  const hoursAt = (f: number) => (f <= 0.6 ? H3D * f / 0.6 : H3D * Math.exp(((f - 0.6) / 0.4) * LSPAN));
  // whole hours up to 3 days, whole days after
  const snap = (h: number) => (h < H3D ? Math.round(h) : Math.round(h / 24) * 24);
  // piecewise-linear in plot position through [hours, value] anchors
  const interp = (h: number, pts: [number, number][]) => {
    const f = frac(h);
    for (let i = 1; i < pts.length; i++) {
      const fa = frac(pts[i - 1][0]), fb = frac(pts[i][0]);
      if (f <= fb) return pts[i - 1][1] + (pts[i][1] - pts[i - 1][1]) * ((f - fa) / (fb - fa || 1));
    }
    return pts[pts.length - 1][1];
  };

  // Schematic (shape, not data) of who supplies blood glucose, after Cahill's classic picture:
  // the meal first, then liver glycogen and gluconeogenesis sharing the load (about half each
  // at 12 h), then almost all gluconeogenesis by day 2-3. Shares sum to 1.
  const smooth = (a: number, b: number, x: number) => { const t = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (x - a) / (b - a))); return t * t * (3 - 2 * t); };
  function supply(h: number): [number, number, number] {
    const meal = 1 - smooth(1.5, 5, h);
    const glycFrac = 1 / (1 + Math.exp((h - 12) / 4.5));
    return [meal, (1 - meal) * glycFrac, (1 - meal) * (1 - glycFrac)];
  }
  // blood ketone bodies in mM, rounded from the lesson's table (2 h, 12 h, 24 h, 3 d, 5 wk)
  const KET: [number, number][] = [[0, 0.1], [4, 0.1], [12, 0.15], [24, 0.4], [H3D, 2.5], [H5W, 7.5]];
  const KET_MAX = 8;
  // schematic ketone share of the brain's fuel: none to ~24 h, "more" by day 3, about two-thirds at 5 weeks
  const BRAIN_K: [number, number][] = [[0, 0], [24, 0], [H3D, 0.3], [H5W, 2 / 3]];

  const BOUNDS = [0, 4, 24, H3D, H5W];
  const BAND_FILL = [ORANGE, GOLD, ACCENT, PLUM];
  const BAND_LABEL = ['Fed', 'Overnight', 'Fasting', 'Prolonged fast'];
  const TICKS: [number, string][] = [[0, '0'], [4, '4'], [12, '12'], [24, '24 h'], [H3D, '3 d'], [168, '1 wk'], [H5W, '5 wk']];
  const MUTED = '#6b6b6b', GOLD_INK = '#7f6315', ORANGE_INK = '#b35900';

  function draw(svg: SVGElement, h: number, s: State) {
    const W = Math.round(Math.max(300, Math.min(760, svg.getBoundingClientRect().width || 460)));
    const x0 = 36, x1 = W - 14, span = x1 - x0;
    const X = (t: number) => x0 + frac(t) * span;
    const pT = 34, pB = 116;            // stacked-area plot
    const kT = 122, kB = 142;           // ketone strip
    const rT = 147, rB = 160;           // brain-fuel strip
    const bT = 166, bB = 186;           // state band
    const H = 208;
    svg.setAttribute('viewBox', `0 0 ${W} ${H}`);
    while (svg.firstChild) svg.removeChild(svg.firstChild);
    const add = (n: string, a: Record<string, string | number>, t?: string) => { const e = el(n, a); if (t !== undefined) e.textContent = t; svg.appendChild(e); return e; };
    const halo = { stroke: '#fff', 'stroke-width': 2.5, 'paint-order': 'stroke', 'stroke-linejoin': 'round' };

    // --- stacked area: share of blood-glucose supply ---------------------------------------
    add('text', { x: x0, y: 13, fill: NAVY, 'font-size': 11.5, 'font-weight': 700 }, 'Who is supplying blood glucose?');
    add('text', { x: x1, y: 13, 'text-anchor': 'end', fill: MUTED, 'font-size': 10 }, 'schematic');
    const N = 200, hs: number[] = [], pts: [number, number, number][] = [];
    for (let i = 0; i <= N; i++) { const t = hoursAt(i / N); hs.push(t); pts.push(supply(t)); }
    const Y = (f: number) => pB - f * (pB - pT);
    const layer = (lo: (p: [number, number, number]) => number, hi: (p: [number, number, number]) => number, fill: string) => {
      let d = '';
      pts.forEach((p, i) => { d += `${i ? 'L' : 'M'}${X(hs[i]).toFixed(1)},${Y(hi(p)).toFixed(1)}`; });
      for (let i = N; i >= 0; i--) d += `L${X(hs[i]).toFixed(1)},${Y(lo(pts[i])).toFixed(1)}`;
      add('path', { d: d + 'Z', fill, 'fill-opacity': 0.55, stroke: fill, 'stroke-width': 1 });
    };
    layer(() => 0, (p) => p[0], ORANGE);
    layer((p) => p[0], (p) => p[0] + p[1], GOLD);
    layer((p) => p[0] + p[1], () => 1, ACCENT);
    add('line', { x1: x0, y1: pT, x2: x0, y2: pB, stroke: '#b9b9c2', 'stroke-width': 1 });
    // dashed seam where the time axis switches from linear hours to compressed days
    add('line', { x1: X(H3D), y1: pT, x2: X(H3D), y2: bB, stroke: '#9a9aa3', 'stroke-width': 0.8, 'stroke-dasharray': '1 2' });
    // --- current-time marker ----------------------------------------------------------------
    const mx = X(h);
    add('line', { x1: mx, y1: pT - 2, x2: mx, y2: bB + 2, stroke: NAVY, 'stroke-width': 1.6, 'stroke-dasharray': '3 2' });
    add('circle', { cx: mx, cy: pT - 2, r: 4.5, fill: s.color, stroke: '#fff', 'stroke-width': 1.5, 'data-knob': 1 });
    add('text', { x: x0 - 5, y: pT + 4, 'text-anchor': 'end', fill: MUTED, 'font-size': 10 }, '100%');
    add('text', { x: x0 - 5, y: pB, 'text-anchor': 'end', fill: MUTED, 'font-size': 10 }, '0');
    // in-area labels, placed where each source is thickest
    add('text', { x: X(1.2), y: pT - 5, fill: ORANGE_INK, 'font-size': 10.5, 'font-weight': 700 }, '↓ the meal');
    add('text', { x: Math.max(x0 + 4, X(5)), y: Y(0.14), fill: GOLD_INK, 'font-size': 11, 'font-weight': 700, ...halo }, 'liver glycogen');
    add('text', { x: X(H3D), y: Y(0.55), 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: NAVY, 'font-size': 11.5, 'font-weight': 700 }, 'new glucose (gluconeogenesis)');

    // --- ketone strip (mM, rising to about 7-8 mM at 5 weeks) -------------------------------
    const kY = (mm: number) => kB - (mm / KET_MAX) * (kB - kT);
    let kd = `M${X(0)},${kB}`;
    hs.forEach((t) => { kd += `L${X(t).toFixed(1)},${kY(interp(t, KET)).toFixed(1)}`; });
    kd += `L${X(H5W)},${kB}Z`;
    add('path', { d: kd, fill: NAVY, 'fill-opacity': 0.18, stroke: NAVY, 'stroke-width': 1.4 });
    add('text', { x: x0 + 4, y: kT + 10, fill: NAVY, 'font-size': 10.5, 'font-weight': 600, ...halo }, 'blood ketone bodies');
    add('text', { x: X(H3D), y: kT + 8, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: NAVY, 'font-size': 9.5, ...halo }, '2–3 mM');
    add('text', { x: x1 - 2, y: kB - 3, 'text-anchor': 'end', fill: NAVY, 'font-size': 9.5, 'font-weight': 700, ...halo }, '7–8 mM');

    // --- brain-fuel strip: glucose (teal) with the ketone share (navy) growing from below ---
    add('rect', { x: x0, y: rT, width: span, height: rB - rT, fill: ACCENT, 'fill-opacity': 0.3 });
    let rd = `M${X(0)},${rB}`;
    hs.forEach((t) => { rd += `L${X(t).toFixed(1)},${(rB - interp(t, BRAIN_K) * (rB - rT)).toFixed(1)}`; });
    rd += `L${X(H5W)},${rB}Z`;
    add('path', { d: rd, fill: NAVY, 'fill-opacity': 0.55 });
    add('text', { x: x0 + 4, y: rB - 3, fill: NAVY, 'font-size': 9.5, 'font-weight': 600, ...halo }, 'brain burns: glucose');
    add('text', { x: x1 - 2, y: rB - 3, 'text-anchor': 'end', fill: NAVY, 'font-size': 9.5, 'font-weight': 700, ...halo }, '⅔ ketones');

    // --- state band + time ticks --------------------------------------------------------------
    for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
      const sx = X(BOUNDS[i]), ex = X(BOUNDS[i + 1]);
      const on = h >= BOUNDS[i] && (h < BOUNDS[i + 1] || (i === 3 && h === H5W));
      add('rect', { x: sx, y: bT, width: ex - sx, height: bB - bT, fill: BAND_FILL[i], 'fill-opacity': on ? 0.32 : 0.12, stroke: BAND_FILL[i], 'stroke-width': on ? 1.5 : 0.8 });
      if (ex - sx > BAND_LABEL[i].length * 6 + 6) {
        add('text', { x: (sx + ex) / 2, y: bT + 14, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: on ? NAVY : '#4b4b55', 'font-size': 10.5, 'font-weight': on ? 700 : 400 }, BAND_LABEL[i]);
      }
    }
    TICKS.forEach(([t, label]) => {
      if (t === 4 && span < 330) return; // 0 and 4 collide on narrow screens
      add('line', { x1: X(t), y1: bB, x2: X(t), y2: bB + 4, stroke: '#9a9aa3', 'stroke-width': 1 });
      add('text', { x: X(t), y: bB + 15, 'text-anchor': t === H5W ? 'end' : 'middle', fill: MUTED, 'font-size': 10 }, label);
    });
    svg.appendChild(svg.querySelector('[data-knob]')!); // keep the time knob on top
  }

  function fmtTime(h: number): string {
    if (h < 24) return `${h} h`;
    const d = Math.floor(h / 24), r = h % 24;
    if (r === 0 && d >= 7 && d % 7 === 0) return `${d / 7} wk`;
    return r === 0 ? `${d} d` : `${d} d ${r} h`;
  }

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-fedfast]').forEach((root) => {
    const svg = root.querySelector('[data-svg]') as unknown as SVGElement;
    const timeIn = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-in="time"]')!;
    const timeOut = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-out="time"]')!;
    const nameEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-name]')!;
    const hormoneEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-hormone]')!;
    const glucoseEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-glucose]')!;
    const carbonEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-carbon]')!;
    const liverEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-liver]')!;
    const adiposeEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-adipose]')!;
    const muscleEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-muscle]')!;
    const brainEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-brain]')!;
    const max = parseInt(timeIn.max, 10) || 200;
    function render() {
      const h = snap(hoursAt(parseInt(timeIn.value, 10) / max));
      const s = stateFor(h);
      timeOut.textContent = fmtTime(h);
      nameEl.textContent = s.name;
      nameEl.style.color = s.color;
      hormoneEl.textContent = s.hormone;
      glucoseEl.textContent = s.glucose;
      carbonEl.textContent = s.carbon;
      liverEl.textContent = s.liver;
      adiposeEl.textContent = s.adipose;
      muscleEl.textContent = s.muscle;
      brainEl.textContent = s.brain;
      timeIn.setAttribute('aria-valuetext', `${fmtTime(h)} since eating: ${s.name.toLowerCase()}`);
      draw(svg, h, s);
    }
    timeIn.addEventListener('input', render);
    let lastW = 0;
    if ('ResizeObserver' in window) {
      new ResizeObserver(() => {
        const w = Math.round(svg.getBoundingClientRect().width);
        if (w && Math.abs(w - lastW) > 4) { lastW = w; render(); }
      }).observe(svg as unknown as Element);
    }
    render();
  });
</script>

<style>
  .fft { padding: var(--ddp-space-3) var(--ddp-space-4) var(--ddp-space-4); margin: var(--ddp-space-5) 0; }
  .fft-head { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 0.3rem; font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--ddp-text-sm); color: var(--ddp-color-primary); margin-bottom: var(--ddp-space-2); }
  .fft-chip { font-family: var(--ddp-font-mono); font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); font-weight: 400; color: var(--ddp-color-muted); }
  .fft-svg { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ddp-color-accent) 5%, #fff); border: 1px solid var(--ddp-color-line); border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: var(--ddp-space-2); }
  .fft-slabel { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.1rem; font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); margin-bottom: var(--ddp-space-3); }
  .fft-slabel em { font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; color: var(--ddp-color-accent); font-family: var(--ddp-font-mono); }
  .fft-slabel input:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--ddp-color-accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
  .fft-slabel input { accent-color: var(--ddp-color-accent); }
  .fft-state { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 0.1rem 0.75rem; margin-bottom: var(--ddp-space-1); }
  .fft-statename { font-size: var(--ddp-text-lg); font-weight: 700; color: var(--ddp-color-primary); }
  .fft-hormone { font-family: var(--ddp-font-mono); font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-accent); text-align: right; }
  .fft-glucose { margin: 0 0 var(--ddp-space-1); font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); line-height: 1.5; min-height: 3em; padding: var(--ddp-space-2) var(--ddp-space-3); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ddp-color-accent) 8%, transparent); border-radius: 6px; }
  .fft-carbon { margin: 0 0 var(--ddp-space-3); font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); line-height: 1.45; padding: 0 var(--ddp-space-3); }
  .fft-carbon-k { font-family: var(--ddp-font-mono); font-weight: 700; color: var(--ddp-color-secondary-ink); }
  .fft-organs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--ddp-space-2); margin-bottom: var(--ddp-space-3); }
  @media (min-width: 560px) { .fft-organs { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
  .fft-organ { border: 1px solid var(--ddp-color-line); border-radius: 6px; padding: var(--ddp-space-2) var(--ddp-space-3); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.15rem; }
  .fft-o-name { font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); font-weight: 700; font-family: var(--ddp-font-mono); color: var(--ddp-color-secondary-ink); }
  .fft-o-job { font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); line-height: 1.45; }
  .fft-foot { margin: var(--ddp-space-3) 0 0; font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); border-left: 3px solid var(--ddp-color-secondary); padding-left: 0.55rem; }
</style>
